# ██╔═██╗ ██║  ██║██║   ██║╚════██║
# ██║  ██╗██████╔╝╚██████╔╝███████║
# ╚═╝  ╚═╝╚═════╝  ╚═════╝ ╚══════╝
# ---------------------------------
#   F2 — the verbs this desktop has, on the file under the cursor.
#
# NORTON COMMANDER'S F2 WAS A TEXT FILE OF COMMANDS a person had written, and
# mc's is this one. It is empty on a stock image, which means F2 opens a menu
# with nothing in it — a key that does nothing teaches that the key is broken.
#
# EVERY LINE NAMES A PROGRAM THAT IS ON THE IMAGE, and `testing/preflight.sh`
# refuses one that is not. A text file has no `show` callback: a row here
# cannot hide itself when its program is missing, so a verb that is still being
# built does not belong in this file until it ships.
#
# ONE LETTER, THEN THE TITLE, THEN TAB-INDENTED COMMAND LINES. mc runs the
# block as `/bin/sh` and WAITS for it, so anything that opens a window of its
# own is backgrounded — the same rule the extension file keeps.
#
# `%f` is the file under the cursor and `%d` the panel's directory; both are
# quoted by mc before the script sees them.
# ---------------------------------

shell_patterns=0

o       Open with the desktop's handler
        (kdos-appbox open %f &)

k       Show this file in Dolphin
        (dolphin --select %f &)

e       Edit here
        ${EDITOR-nano} %f

f       Find in this folder
        (kfind %d &)

t       Terminal here
        (konsole --workdir %d &)

p       Add this folder to Places
        kdos places add %d

s       Share this file to another machine
        kdos-share %f

r       Move to trash
        kdos trash %f

g       Git status here
        cd %d && lazygit
